{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF2", "text": "I have a finding from infrastructure. During today's roster reconciliation, I confirmed that Omar is the only engineer currently authorized to execute storage failback, and he is available for the rollback coverage window only from 1:00 AM to 5:00 AM. The roster document still lists Marta for that coverage, which is a gap we need to address before publishing."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF3", "text": "I have a finding from customer support. While reviewing the Northstar support agreement for another account matter this morning, I confirmed that any search degradation requires customer status updates every 30 minutes, not every 60 minutes, and that Support must own those updates. I have not updated the rollout ticket yet. The current draft roster calls for updates every 60 minutes, which does not meet the Northstar agreement requirement."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "No concerns from backend engineering. Swapping Marta to primary and Leo to secondary addresses the rollback access gap directly, since Marta has current rollback access. I'll file the access ticket for Leo's rollback access as a follow-up, as you proposed. We're good on my end."}
```

